> API and interpretation

Every row and finite input is validated before allocation. Queries require
ordered nonempty inclusive bounds within the grid; empty grids cannot be
queried. Actual nonfinite prefix/query arithmetic fails. Const table/query
accessors borrow owned storage for the table lifetime. The four-query original
example is retained; exhaustive rectangle agreement is verified independently
rather than asserted from an unretained old receipt.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

